      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3}\\), we will first use the exponent rules to simplify the expression.\n\n### Step 1: Apply the exponent rule \\((a^m)^n = a^{mn}\\)\nWe rewrite \\(2^7\\) and \\(3^3\\) using the rule mentioned above:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^7 \\cdot 3^3} = \\sqrt[4]{2^{7 \\cdot 4} \\cdot 3^{3 \\cdot 4}}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt[4]{2^{28} \\cdot 3^{12}}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Simplify the exponents\nNow, we simplify the exponents inside the radical:\n\\[\n2^{28} = (2^4)^7 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3^{12} = (3^3)^4\n\\]\nHowever, for the fourth root, we use:\n\\[\n2^{28} = 2^4 \\cdot 2^{24} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3^{12} = 3^3 \\cdot 3^9\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Group the like bases under the fourth root\nNow, we combine these groups under the fourth root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{2^{28} \\cdot 3^{12}} = \\sqrt[4]{(2^4 \\cdot 2^{24}) \\cdot 3^{12}}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Simplify the group under the fourth root\nWe simplify each group separately:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[4]{(2^4 \\cdot 2^{24}) \\cdot 3^{12}} = \\sqrt[4]{4^4 \\cdot 2^4 \\cdot 2^{20} \\cdot 3^{12}}\n\\]\n\nNow, we use the exponent rule again to combine the exponents:\n\\[\n4^4 = (2^2)^4 = 2^8\n\\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n2^8 \\cdot 2^4 \\cdot 2^{20} \\cdot 3^{12}\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Simplify the combined exponents\nCombine the exponents for the prime factors:\n\\[\n2^{8 + 4 + 20} \\cdot 3^{12} = 2^{32/4} \\cdot 3^{12} = 2^8 \\cdot 3^{12}\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Apply the suggested notation\nThe expression can now be written in the form \\(a \\sqrt[4]{b}\\):\n\\[\n2^8 \\cdot 3^{12} = 2^4 \\cdot 2^4 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 3^9 = (2^4 \\cdot 2^4) \\cdot (\\sqrt[4]{3^9})^4 = (2^8 \\cdot 3^3) \\sqrt[4]{3^{12}}\n\\]\nThe simplified form is \\(a \\sqrt[4]{b}\\) where \\(a = 2^4 \\cdot 3^3\\) and \\(b = 3^{12}\\).\n\n### Step 7: Compute the final values\nCalculate \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\\[\na = 2^4 \\cdot 3^3 = 16 \\cdot 27 = 432\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 3^{12} = 531441\n\\]\n\n### Step 8: Compute \\(a + b\\)\nCompute the sum:\n\\[\na + b = 432 + 531441 = 531873\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(a + b\\) is \\(\\boxed{531873}\\).",
